From 8f9ed480c3179a648c84494a7035f0fe62af40c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy J Fontaine <tjfontaine@atxconsulting.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 06:45:36 -0700
Subject: bifrost: aggregation, speculation, fault accounting, and vtimestamp
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five workstreams in one commit for atomic application.

W3 — per-CPU fault accounting in fault-prone kfuncs.
  bifrost_kfunc_note_fault() inlined; called from copyin /
  copyinstr / strlen / strchr / strrchr / strstr / progenyof
  error paths to bump the per-CPU
  BIFROST_DROP_CLASS_DBLERR counter.  Surfaces in the host
  CLI's drop summary as `dblerr=N`.

W5a — bifrost_kfunc_clear_agg(struct bpf_map *map__map).
  `__map` suffix routes through the verifier's
  KF_ARG_PTR_TO_MAP path.  Walks every per-CPU value slot of
  the agg map (PERCPU_ARRAY by index, PERCPU_HASH via
  map_get_next_key) and zeroes it.

W5b/W5c — AGG_KIND_LQUANTIZE=5 / AGG_KIND_LLQUANTIZE=6 added
  to the vendored wire.rs (CANONICAL_SHA256 refreshed to
  f565fc5b5adac79d7882abd84eab80f94304e651b3a4878267b3303ba2d3babf).
  The map shape matches quantize (PERCPU_ARRAY of u32-keyed
  bucket counts); the host-side renderer differentiates via
  the AGG_KIND_* discriminant and the per-agg parameter tuple
  registered at compile time.

W8 — real speculation lifecycle:
  - struct bifrost_spec_state declared above
    bifrost_shmem_reserve_kernel_class so the reserve path
    can detect an active speculation lane.
  - Per-CPU buffer of 16 records × 1024 bytes each
    (~16 KB/CPU, ≤ 256 KB cluster-wide on
    BIFROST_NUM_CPUS_MAX = 16).
  - bifrost_shmem_reserve_kernel_class routes into the side
    buffer when active_lane != 0.
  - bifrost_kfunc_speculation allocates lane id 1, refusing
    when a lane is already active.
  - bifrost_kfunc_speculate(id) flips the active flag.
  - bifrost_kfunc_commit(id) deactivates and replays each
    buffered record back through reserve + submit in the
    principal path.
  - bifrost_kfunc_discard(id) zeroes and deactivates.

W10 — bifrost_kfunc_vtimestamp_ns returns
  `current->se.sum_exec_runtime` instead of aliasing
  ktime_get_ns.  DTrace's "ns the current thread has been
  running on a CPU" semantic, sourced directly from the
  kernel scheduler's per-task runtime accounting.

Signed-off-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
